function COMPONENT(request : dval) {
    var page := dval({source_page: ""})
    page["source_page"] = "capy-03-values-and-types"
    page["kind"] = "guide"
    page["slug"] = "values-and-types"
    page["route"] = "/doc/guide/values-and-types/"
    page["title"] = "3. Types"
    page["content"] = "Every Capy value has a type. The compiler checks types before the program runs. It usually infers the type of a local value.\n\n## Integers\n\nAn integer literal has type `s32` when no other type is stated:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var answer := 42\n    print(answer, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\n42\n\n```\n\nState a wider type on the local, or construct the value explicitly:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var signed : s64 = 8\n    var inferred_signed := s64(9)\n    var unsigned : u64 = 10\n    var inferred_unsigned := u64(11)\n    print(signed, \" \", inferred_signed, \" \", unsigned, \" \", inferred_unsigned, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nBoth forms produce the stated wide integer type. `var signed : s64 = s64(8)` also compiles, but the constructor repeats information already supplied by the annotation.\n\nParameters, function results, assignments, typed arrays, struct fields, and the other operand in an expression can also state the integer type. Thus, a function that accepts `u64` can receive the plain literal `8`. An unconstrained literal remains `s32`.\n\nArithmetic requires operands of the same type. Use a constructor when the surrounding code does not state the required type.\n\n## Booleans and floating-point numbers\n\nA `bool` is either `true` or `false`. Conditions require a boolean value.\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var enabled := true\n    var ratio := 2.5\n    print(enabled, \" \", ratio, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nA decimal point or exponent makes an `f64` literal.\n\n## Strings\n\nA `string` stores bytes:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := \"Ada\"\n    var empty := \"\"\n    print(name, empty, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nAn empty string is still a string value. It is not missing data.\n\n## Arrays, tuples, and structs\n\nAn array contains values of one t"
    page["content"] = string(page["content"], "") + "ype:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var names := [\"Ada\", \"Grace\"]\n    print(names[0], \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nA tuple has a fixed number of positions, which can have different types:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var point := (3, 4)\n    print(point[0], \" \", point[1], \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nA struct gives names to fixed fields:\n\n```capy\nstruct Point {\n    x : s32\n    y : s32\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var point := Point(3, 4)\n    print(point.x, \" \", point.y, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nArrays and struct instances are mutable reference values inside one workspace. Assignment shares their identity. Tuples remain immutable.\n\nThe collections chapter covers these types in detail.\n\n## Dynamic values and none\n\nA `dval` holds data whose shape is known only at run time. The `none` value represents missing dynamic data:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var profile := {name: \"Ada\"}\n    var missing := none\n    print(profile.name, \" \", missing?, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\n`none` is different from `\"\"`, `false`, an empty map, and an empty list. A `dval` is also a mutable reference value inside one workspace. The dynamic-values chapter explains mutation, safe reads, and conversions.\n\n## Type aliases\n\nA type alias gives another name to a type:\n\n```capy\ntype Count = s64\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var total : Count = 12\n    print(total, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nAn alias does not create a new runtime type.\n"
    page["label"] = "3. Types"
    page["capy_sig_lines"] = dval([])
    page["param_lines"] = dval([])
    page["notes"] = dval([])
    page["warnings"] = dval([])
    page["see"] = dval([{label: "4. Expressions and control flow", href: "/doc/guide/expressions-and-control-flow/"}, {label: "7. Arrays, tuples, and structs", href: "/doc/guide/collections-and-records/"}, {label: "8. Dynamic values", href: "/doc/guide/dynamic-values/"}, {label: "dvalue", href: "/doc/type/dvalue/"}, {label: "bool", href: "/doc/api/bool/"}, {label: "s32", href: "/doc/api/s32/"}, {label: "s64", href: "/doc/api/s64/"}, {label: "u64", href: "/doc/api/u64/"}, {label: "f64", href: "/doc/api/f64/"}, {label: "string", href: "/doc/api/string/"}, {label: "dval", href: "/doc/api/dval/"}, {label: "length", href: "/doc/api/length/"}])
    page["examples"] = dval([])
    page["guide_examples"] = dval([{entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var answer := 42\n    print(answer, \"\\n\")\n}\n", output: "42\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var signed : s64 = 8\n    var inferred_signed := s64(9)\n    var unsigned : u64 = 10\n    var inferred_unsigned := u64(11)\n    print(signed, \" \", inferred_signed, \" \", unsigned, \" \", inferred_unsigned, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var enabled := true\n    var ratio := 2.5\n    print(enabled, \" \", ratio, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var name := \"Ada\"\n    var empty := \"\"\n    print(name, empty, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var names := [\"Ada\", \"Grace\"]\n    print(names[0], \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var point := (3, 4)\n    print(point[0], \" \", point[1], \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "struct Point {\n    x : s32\n    y : s32\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var point := Point(3, 4)\n    print(point.x, \" \", point.y, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var profile := {name: \"Ada\"}\n    var missing := none\n    print(profile.name, \" \", missing?, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "type Count = s64\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var total : Count = 12\n    print(total, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}])
    component_render("/doc/components/doc_page.capy", page)
}
